---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ObservationField from '../components/ObservationField.astro';
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Fidret — Trust earned."
  description="Expertise that earns trust through sound judgment, useful work and reliable delivery. Developing our first practice in Physical AI."
  canonical="https://fidret.com/"
>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="home-hero shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="hero-context">Trust earned.</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Intelligence meets the real world.</h1>
        <p class="hero-intro">Sound judgment. Useful work. Reliable delivery. We’re building Fidret around expertise people can rely on.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button" href="#physical-ai">Discover our first practice</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/approach/">What guides us</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ObservationField />
      <div class="hero-footnote"><span>Developing our first practice in Physical AI</span><a href="#physical-ai" aria-label="Read about Physical AI"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v16m-6-6 6 6 6-6" /></svg></a></div>
    </section>

    <section id="physical-ai" class="practice-section inverse" aria-labelledby="practice-title">
      <div class="shell practice-grid">
        <div class="practice-heading">
          <p class="section-context">Our first practice</p>
          <h2 id="practice-title">The world is physical.<br />So is the challenge.</h2>
          <p class="practice-lead">Physical AI connects observations of the world with decisions and actions within it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="practice-detail">
          <p>That means working with more than a model. Sensors, timing, changing conditions, integration and the people operating a system all shape what it can reliably do.</p>
          <p>We’re developing this practice through focused questions, reproducible experiments and evidence with its limits intact.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/approach/">How we build confidence</a>
          <p class="practice-status"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>A practice in development. Each step has to earn the next.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="practice-questions" aria-label="Questions shaping the practice">
          <div><span class="question-symbol" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40"><circle cx="20" cy="20" r="11"/><circle cx="20" cy="20" r="3"/><path d="M20 2v7m0 22v7M2 20h7m22 0h7"/></svg></span><h3>What can we observe?</h3><p>The signal, its quality and the conditions around it.</p></div>
          <div><span class="question-symbol" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40"><path d="M5 29h30M8 23l8-10 8 6 8-13"/><circle cx="16" cy="13" r="2"/><circle cx="24" cy="19" r="2"/></svg></span><h3>What does the evidence support?</h3><p>A result is useful when its conditions and limits are clear.</p></div>
          <div><span class="question-symbol" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40"><path d="M9 7h22v26H9zM15 14h10m-10 6h10m-10 6h5"/></svg></span><h3>Who owns what happens next?</h3><p>Responsibility, supervision and recovery belong in the design.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="home-workbench shell" aria-labelledby="workbench-title">
      <div class="workbench-intro">
        <div><p class="section-context">On the workbench</p><h2 id="workbench-title">A small question.<br />A revealing experiment.</h2></div>
        <p>When a sensor reading arrives late, should a system still trust it? Explore the difference between receiving a signal and having one you can use.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="experiment-preview" href="/explorations/signal-freshness/">
        <div class="experiment-copy"><span class="experiment-kind">Synthetic software exploration</span><h3>How fresh is<br />fresh enough?</h3><p>Follow a signal through silence, delay and recovery.</p><span class="experiment-action">Open the walkthrough <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6" /></svg></span></div>
        <div class="signal-preview" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="preview-clock"><span>Observation time</span><span>Arrival time</span></div>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 580 265"><path class="preview-guide" d="M36 56H544M36 201H544M36 128H544"/><path class="preview-tick" d="M76 48v16m106-16v16m106-16v16m106-16v16M76 193v16m106-16v16m106-16v16m106-16v16m106-16v16"/><path class="preview-good" d="M76 56L130 201M182 56L236 201M394 56L448 201"/><path class="preview-delay" d="M288 56L500 201"/><g class="preview-node"><circle cx="76" cy="56" r="6"/><circle cx="182" cy="56" r="6"/><circle cx="394" cy="56" r="6"/><circle cx="130" cy="201" r="6"/><circle cx="236" cy="201" r="6"/><circle cx="448" cy="201" r="6"/></g><g class="preview-late-node"><circle cx="288" cy="56" r="6"/><circle cx="500" cy="201" r="6"/></g><path class="preview-annotation" d="M385 122h78"/><text x="385" y="105" class="preview-label">Late arrival</text></svg>
          <div class="preview-explanation"><span class="preview-key" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Arrival alone doesn’t make an observation current.</span></div>
        </div>
      </a>
      <div class="workbench-footer"><p>A fixed, synthetic walkthrough of our local prototype. No live sensors or hardware claims.</p><a class="text-link" href="/lab/">More from Fidret Lab</a></div>
    </section>

    <section id="purpose" class="purpose-section shell" aria-labelledby="purpose-title">
      <div class="purpose-statement"><p class="section-context">The company we’re building</p><h2 id="purpose-title">Trust comes from<br />what you experience.</h2><p class="editorial">Trust earned.</p></div>
      <div class="purpose-copy"><p>Understanding the real need. Making commitments clear. Following through on the work. That is how we intend to earn our place.</p><p>Fidret is inspired by the Latin <i lang="la">fīdere</i> — to trust, or to rely upon. Our first practice is Physical AI. Our purpose is broader: expertise people can depend on.</p><a class="text-link" href="/approach/">Read our approach</a></div>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
